Audio Deck is distributed under two licences, split by component.

BACKEND  ->  GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0)

    Covers everything except the user interface: the domain, application
    and infrastructure layers together with the CLI, main.py, the build
    scripts and the tests. In the source tree that is src/domain,
    src/application, src/infrastructure and src/cli, plus src/main.py.
    Full text: LICENSE-GPL-3.0.txt

USER INTERFACE  ->  GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0 (LGPL-3.0)

    Covers the PySide6 and Qt layer (src/presentation), licensed under the
    LGPL to align with Qt's own licensing. Full text:
    LICENSE-LGPL-3.0.txt, which incorporates the terms of the GPL-3.0 in
    LICENSE-GPL-3.0.txt.

The running application shows both under its Help menu: "UI Licence
(LGPL-3.0)" and "Backend Licence (GPL-3.0)".

